    <div class="page-header education">
        <h1 class="page-header-ttl">International Education Programs</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="page-body">
        <main>
            <div class="breadcrumb">
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/">Home</a></li>
                                            <li><a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/education/">International Education Programs</a></li>
                        <li>JOY Program (Exchange Program)</li>
                                    </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="main-inner">
                <article>
                    <div class="article-head">
                                                    <h2 class="ttl">JOY Program (Exchange Program)</h2>
                                                                    </div>
                    <div class="article-body">
                                                                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-1">
                                    
                                                                            
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p><strong>This program is for students who are enrolled in an undergraduate degree program at a university that has signed a mutual student exchange agreement with YNU.</strong></p>
<p><em>≪Contact Information≫<br />
<strong>Student Exchange Section<br />
Email：global.exchange@ynu.ac.jp</strong></em></p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                    </div>
                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-2">
                                                                            <div class="article-content-ttl">
                                            <h3>Junior Year Overseas at Yokohama National University (JOY) Program</h3>
                                        </div>
                                    
                                                                            
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>In October 1997, the International Student Center started the JOY Program for students from partner universities outside Japan to give them the opportunity to experience Japanese university life for up to a year. The outline of JOY is as follows:</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                    </div>
                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-3">
                                                                            <div class="article-content-ttl">
                                            <h3>JOY Program Overview</h3>
                                        </div>
                                    
                                                                                                                        <h4>Objective</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>To assist international students coming to Yokohama National University under student-exchange agreements by providing them with the opportunity to acquire a good understanding of Japan and its role in the international community.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Eligibility</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Students must be enrolled full-time in an <strong>undergraduate degree program at a university that has signed a mutual student exchange agreement with YNU.</strong></p>
<p>Students must be proficient in English (<strong>TOEFL iBT 80(Pre-January 2026 scoring system)/ 4.0(Post-January 2026 scoring system), IELTS 6.0 or higher*</strong>) or Japanese (<strong>JLPT N2 or higher</strong>).</p>
<p>*English Certificates other than official TOEFL and IELTS scores are accepted with a letter from the home university certifying the English proficiency equivalent/higher to TOEFL iBT 4.0, IELTS 6.0 or CEFR B2 level.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Educational Program</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Courses are offered in varieties of disciplines covering humanities, social sciences, and engineering in English specifically for JOY Program students. They may also attend other courses offered by the faculties, provided they have adequate language skills and approval from the lecturers in charge.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Scholarships</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>JOY students are eligible to apply for the Japan Student Services Association (JASSO) scholarship. The application form is included in the JOY Program application packet. The JASSO scholarship consists of JPY 80,000/month stipends.<br />
Given the limited number of JASSO scholarships and the increasing number of JOY applicants, this scholarship is increasingly competitive. If available, students should pursue scholarship opportunities at their home universities.However, <strong>JASSO rules stipulate that students cannot simultaneously receive the JASSO scholarship and any other study abroad scholarship exceeding JPY 80,000/month (the sum of other scholarships excluding travel support).</strong></p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Nomination</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Students need to be first officially nominated by their home university.<br />
We will inform partner universities of the details for the nomination procedures and deadlines.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Application</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>After receiving the nomination, we will send the application link directly to the student.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>Admission</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Students will be selected and admitted on the basis of the quality of their application documents, and on the student exchange balance between their home universities and YNU.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                        <h4>JOY Program Timetables</h4>
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>2026 Class Schedule<br />
<a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/05/Web掲載分-Spring-2026-JOY-Timetable.pdf">Spring</a></p>
<p>2025 Class Schedule<br />
<a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/04/★WEB掲載分20250410-Spring-2025l-JOY-Program-Timetable.pdf">Spring</a><br />
<a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/10/Web-掲載分-20251015JOY-Timetable-.pdf">Fall</a></p>
<p>2024 Class Schedule<br />
<a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/05/★20240515-JOY-Timetable　加工分2024SOCRATES_JOY_TimetableList.pdf">Spring</a><br />
<a href="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/2024-Fall-JOY-Program-Timetable.pdf">Fall</a></p>
<p><a href="https://risyu.jmk.ynu.ac.jp/gakumu_portal/Public/Syllabus/">Syllabus</a></p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                    </div>
                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-4">
                                    
                                                                            
                                                                                    <h5>On Arrival Campus Tour of 2026 Fall Exchange Program</h5>
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>On-arrival Campus Tour of Exchange Program for the 2026 Fall was held on October 1st (Thu).<br />
Forty exchange students from thirty universities in eighteen countries/regions started the 2026 Fall Exchange Program at Yokohama National University.<br />
During the On Arrival Campus Tour, the exchange students were divided into small groups and walked around the campus together with students of Yokohama National University and continuing exchange students from the 2026 Spring.<br />
Through the On Arrival Campus Tour, they prepared for their new life at Yokohama National University.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="img">
                                                    <img src="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/01/20261001_024914300_iOS-scaled.jpg" >
                                                                                                    </div>
                                                                                    
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                    </div>
                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-5">
                                    
                                                                            
                                                                                    <h5>Congratulations on completing the 2026 Spring JOY Program!</h5>
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Forty-five exchange students from thirty universities in seventeen countries/regions completed the 2026 Spring JOY Program and go back to their home universities after this semester.<br />
On August 5th (Wed), the last day of the program, each of JOY Program students gave a one-minute speech at the International Student Center to share their memories and experiences during the exchange.<br />
It seemed that they still do not want to say goodbye to Yokohama National University and many of the valuable encounters they had in Japan.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="img">
                                                    <img src="https://global.ynu.ac.jp/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/01/Spring-2026-YNU-Exchange-Program-Closing-Ceremony-Group-Photo-scaled-e1790925946262.jpg" >
                                                                                                    </div>
                                                                                    
                                                                                
                                        
                                        
                                                                    </div>
                                                            <div class="article-content" id="section-6">
                                    
                                                                            
                                                                                    <h5>JOY program student introduced his country's culture</h5>
                                        
                                                                                                                                    <p>Mr. Heinrich of the JOY program student introduced German culture to YNU students and faculty staff.<br />
He introduced about transportation in Germany, German food and drinks and party games with a a lot of pictures and gestures.<br />
He also shared his university life, including classes and the cafeteria.<br />
About 30 participants enjoyed learning about the differences between German and Japanese culture and university life.</p>
                                                                                    
                                        
                                        
